---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://akturesult.bond";
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}/guides/aktu-cgpa-calculation`;

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "@id": pageUrl,
      "url": pageUrl,
      "headline": "AKTU CGPA Calculation & Percentage Conversion: Official Ordinance Guide",
      "description": "Learn how AKTU calculates Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA), how to convert CGPA to percentage using ((CGPA - 0.75) × 10), and division rules.",
      "datePublished": "2026-03-20T08:00:00+05:30",
      "dateModified": "2026-10-16T12:00:00+05:30",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond Student Editorial Team"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond",
        "url": siteUrl
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${pageUrl}/#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": siteUrl },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": `${siteUrl}/guides` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "CGPA Calculation", "item": pageUrl }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout 
  title="AKTU CGPA Calculation & Percentage Formula ((CGPA-0.75)*10) | akturesult.bond"
  description="Master AKTU CGPA calculation and percentage conversion. Learn the official university formula, division criteria (Distinction, 1st, 2nd), and worked examples."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-black light:bg-white text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-gray-300 light:text-gray-800 font-semibold truncate">CGPA Calculation</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border pb-6 mb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-brand-blue font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
          <span>Official Ordinance</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>6 min read</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Updated October 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white light:text-ink leading-tight">
          AKTU CGPA Calculation &amp; Percentage Conversion Formula
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Need to convert your AKTU CGPA to percentage for campus placements, GATE, CAT, or government jobs? Here is the official statutory formula and division classification rules.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mandatory Non-Affiliation Alert -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
        <strong>Important Student Notice:</strong> akturesult.bond is an independent student utility platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU). This conversion guide reflects the official notification issued by the AKTU Academic Council.
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            1. What is CGPA?
          </h2>
          <p>
            <strong>CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point Average)</strong> represents the cumulative academic performance of a student across all semesters completed to date. While SGPA measures performance in a single term, CGPA is the weighted aggregate used for graduation rankings, degree awards, and corporate recruitment eligibility.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            2. The Official AKTU CGPA Formula
          </h2>
          <p>
            CGPA is computed by weighting each semester's SGPA by the total credits registered in that semester:
          </p>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-canvas-dark-tile light:bg-canvas-light-tile border border-brand-blue/30 text-center space-y-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">
              CGPA = &Sigma; (C<sub>j</sub> &times; SGPA<sub>j</sub>) / &Sigma; C<sub>j</sub>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
              Where <strong>C<sub>j</sub></strong> is the total credits registered in semester <em>j</em>, and <strong>SGPA<sub>j</sub></strong> is the SGPA achieved in semester <em>j</em>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            3. Converting AKTU CGPA to Percentage (%)
          </h2>
          <p>
            A common misconception among students is multiplying CGPA directly by 10 (or 9.5 as used by CBSE). Under the statutory circular approved by the AKTU Academic Council, the mandatory formula is:
          </p>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-canvas-dark-tile light:bg-canvas-light-tile border border-emerald-500/30 text-center space-y-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-emerald-400">
              Equivalent Percentage (%) = (CGPA - 0.75) &times; 10
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
              Official AKTU Formula (Applicable to all B.Tech, B.Pharm, MBA, MCA, and M.Tech students).
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Quick Conversion Table -->
          <div class="overflow-x-auto pt-2">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-canvas-dark-surface light:bg-canvas-light-surface text-white light:text-ink">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">CGPA</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Calculation Step</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Official Percentage Equivalent</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-canvas-dark-border/40 light:divide-canvas-light-border font-mono">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">9.50</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(9.50 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">87.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">9.00</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(9.00 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">82.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">8.50</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(8.50 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">77.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">8.00</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(8.00 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">72.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">7.50</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(7.50 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-400">67.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">7.00</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(7.00 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">62.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">6.50</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(6.50 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-cyan-400">57.50%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">6.00</td>
                  <td class="p-3">(6.00 - 0.75) &times; 10</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-amber-400">52.50%</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            4. AKTU Degree Division Award Classifications
          </h2>
          <p>
            When you complete your degree program, AKTU awards divisions according to the following thresholds:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 space-y-2">
              <span class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-sm block">First Division with Honours</span>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                Requires <strong>CGPA &ge; 7.50</strong> AND passing all subjects across all semesters in the <strong>first attempt</strong> without any carry-over (COP) or grace marks (PWG).
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-blue/30 bg-brand-blue/10 space-y-2">
              <span class="font-bold text-brand-blue text-sm block">First Division</span>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                Awarded to students graduating with <strong>CGPA &ge; 6.50</strong> across all completed credit semesters.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border bg-canvas-dark-surface/60 space-y-2">
              <span class="font-bold text-white light:text-ink text-sm block">Second Division</span>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
                Awarded to students graduating with <strong>5.00 &le; CGPA &lt; 6.50</strong>. Minimum 5.00 CGPA is required to be awarded the degree.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

      <!-- Quick CTA -->
      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue/20 to-purple-600/15 border border-brand-blue/30 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Check your official SGPA and CGPA</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">Inspect your complete semester grades grid on OneView.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue-hover text-white text-xs font-bold transition-all shadow-md shrink-0">
          ⚡ Check Your CGPA &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
